1
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:29,897
Every time the rain no longer falls, and I
see the sky, I think the rain is falling.

2
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,277
Back to when I was a child.

3
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,937
Who could only cry?

4
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:37,497
Blindly chasing after him.

5
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:42,317
I fell far behind my only thought.

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,377
One day I will be stronger.

7
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,897
Bridery and gratitude.

8
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:50,497
Fading with the wind.

9
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:53,317
Am I stronger now than I was before?

10
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:55,297
Or as weak as back then?

11
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,397
I don't know for sure.

12
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:01,157
But until I do, my voyage will not end.

13
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:06,340
No matter what's next, I'm
walking straight ahead.

14
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:12,577
So let's go, there's nothing
that can stop us now.

15
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:17,560
Though time's all on our side,
we'll never let it pull us down.

16
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:22,577
And we may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

17
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:27,180
There's no way anything
will take what I hope.

18
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:33,677
The voices inside me push
me to keep surviving.

19
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:39,257
I'll go on, I'll get through,
no matter what I gotta do.

20
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:43,177
The fiercest storms of
all can pour upon me.

21
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:48,380
I don't care why in the
world would I turn back?

22
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:54,857
So let's go,

23
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:56,980
there's nothing that can stop.

24
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:02,837
The tides that are on our side
will never let it pull us down.

25
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:07,897
And we may fall, but we'll
always keep on standing.

26
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:14,097
There's no way anything will take
what I hold dear away from me.

27
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,740
I know the future's there for us to see.

28
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:30,037
This Marine Ford business
is gonna change the world!

29
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,473
So it's true after all!

30
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,457
The news spread like wildfire falling on
ears that could scarcely believe the words.

31
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:41,560
Ace, son of the great gold Roger, fell
in battle alongside Whitebeard. Extra!

32
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,760
Get ready to issue an extra!

33
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,198
We just received some breaking news.

34
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:49,680
Whitebeard was killed
shortly after Firefist Ace,

35
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,016
and the Marines have claimed victory.

36
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,700
He's really dead.

37
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,110
Yeah!

38
00:02:55,193 --> 00:02:56,023
Yeah!

39
00:02:56,106 --> 00:02:57,200
This crew is done for!

40
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:58,557
There's peace again!

41
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,757
If the Navy can take care of Whitebeard!

42
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,252
Then the rest of the pirates will follow!

43
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:05,480
While many celebrated,

44
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:10,980
those who saw these events unfold
with their own eyes stand transfixed,

45
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,700
their mouths agape,?

46
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:15,280
words frozen on their lips.

47
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:24,480
Bon voyage, Whitebeard.

48
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,477
His name was Edward Newgate.

49
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:32,137
In his prime, he stood against
even the king of the pirates.

50
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:34,457
His crew was his family.

51
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:38,160
And he fought beside them
into the ripe old age of 72.

52
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:41,620
The world knew him as Whitebeard.

53
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:45,577
He had stepped boldly into
Marineford and brought

54
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:48,077
the walls of the Navy
headquarters down around him.

55
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:50,860
And yet, despite his superhuman efforts,

56
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:53,887
the Navy forces, aided
by the Seven Warlords,

57
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,520
proved too strong?

58
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:58,000
Ah, what a day!

59
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:00,145
It's the birth of a new world,

60
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:05,217
or the death of an old one I think today's
party may have some life in it yet.

61
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,460
That bastard!

62
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:10,897
Marco, for what it's worth,
we all share your sentiment.

63
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:13,020
But it's not the time for revenge.

64
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:15,540
Yeah, I get it. Let's go.

65
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:19,873
Save your tears and hurry up, you fools.

66
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,529
You haven't forgotten your
captain's final orders, have you?

67
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:25,340
No distractions.

68
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,937
We'll be setting sail
as quickly as we can.

69
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:28,850
Understood.

70
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,659
That old Carter was tough as nails.

71
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,351
I thought he'd never die.

72
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:39,057
A minor delay, yes, but
scarcely unexpected.

73
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:40,840
Now for the fun part.

74
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:46,194
Yeah, let's give them a magic
show they'll never forget!

75
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:55,217
Be careful, who knows
what they're planning!

76
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,130
You monster!

77
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:58,322
Haven't you done enough to Pops?

78
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:03,699
Watch carefully, it's a good trick!

79
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:08,540
So good, in fact, it's gonna shake
the whole world down to its core!

80
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:11,422
Whatever this is, it's not good.

81
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:14,836
Is he doing something to
Whitebeard's corpse in there?

82
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:16,460
Now, now.

83
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:19,637
I know you're curious, but
please don't interrupt.

84
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,377
Don't get too cocky, pirates!

85
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:24,237
He joined the seven warlords
just so he could betray us.

86
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:27,261
Whatever he's up to, you
can bet it won't be good.

87
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,540
I can't wait.

88
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:33,240
So what happens if this plan
doesn't work? We disband.

89
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:48,730
Hey!

90
00:05:48,813 --> 00:05:49,717
Hey, where are you going?

91
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,630
Captain!

92
00:05:50,713 --> 00:05:52,208
Where do you think, stupid?

93
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,226
Someplace far away from here!

94
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:57,066
My plan to kill Whitebeard
is shot, obviously!

95
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,634
So we're running away?

96
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,380
I was so close!

97
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:03,000
Yeah, I'm scared! I admit it!

98
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,857
I'd rather dig a hole, crawl in,

99
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:08,940
and live the rest of my measurable
life in there than face this guy!

100
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:12,957
I don't care if you think
I'm pathetic, dammit!

101
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:15,275
I don't need you losers around anyway!

102
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,560
Captain Buggy! He's crying.

103
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,500
Is it our fault? Aha!

104
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:25,037
He's teaching us a lesson about sympathy.

105
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,897
Seeing Whitebeard
suffering filled him with

106
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:29,437
pity and humanity triumphed over savagery.

107
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:30,350
Beautiful!

108
00:06:30,433 --> 00:06:32,720
His message is engraved upon my soul,

109
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:35,177
but he laughed, fearing
we wouldn't understand.

110
00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:37,540
He had a shot at fame and fortune,

111
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:39,237
but he understood that the cost of his

112
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:41,937
personal integrity was
a price too high to pay.

113
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:44,237
Because material gains
are ultimately meaningless

114
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,317
and public acclaim is fleeting
in these trying times.

115
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,777
I've seen the light, Captain.

116
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:50,507
It's as if I've been reborn.

117
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,417
Share more of your wisdom with us.

118
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,720
I'm scared for knowledge. Go away.

119
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,960
Keep moving.

120
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,358
We're almost there.

121
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:08,717
Luffy I know it hurts right now but you
must carry on for in a world without

122
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,277
ace your courage will be needed tomorrow

123
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:17,437
and every day after fire it's a heavy

124
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:24,237
weight but one I'm confident you can bear
Jinbei I know I might not make it out

125
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:29,537
of this alive I'm sorry but if I die

126
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:32,149
would you look after
are my brother for me.

127
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:37,380
I fear you misjudge my character, Ace.

128
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:41,820
I mean no disrespect, but I may
not be as charitable as you think.

129
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:46,697
I'm certain you care for your brother,
but we live in a world of pirates.

130
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:49,720
I offer my aid to those
I hold in high regard?

131
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,540
but only to them.

132
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:54,397
We've got room on this ship over here!

133
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,310
Coming!

134
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:57,290
What the?

135
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,390
Damn it!

136
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,080
And we were so close, too!

137
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,497
You mean we're stuck?

138
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:07,404
Well, we've gotta do something!

139
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:09,370
Aokiji's coming!

140
00:08:09,453 --> 00:08:10,540
Somebody stop him!

141
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:15,780
We have to run! Go!

142
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,997
Did you really think you
could get away from me?

143
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:33,160
Why don't you save yourself some
trouble and let me kill you?

144
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:45,920
Hand over dragons, son, and
I may decide to spare you.

145
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,040
Akainu, I thought Pops killed him.

146
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:51,480
But how did he survive the fall?

147
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:53,417
Did he come out of the ground?

148
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:54,997
His lava powers freak me out.

149
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:58,100
Team bane a generous offer,

150
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:00,877
but I must refuse you
aren't the only tenacious

151
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:03,760
one here I've decided to protect this boy.

152
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:06,740
No matter the cost have it your way then.

153
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,840
I won't ask twice

154
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:18,037
You're not gonna lay a
finger on Straw Hat pops

155
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:22,100
wanted us to protect him
useless cowards out of my way

156
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:27,620
through Empire Faceproof Synthesis!

157
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:32,520
If I may, I believe I can
be of assistance here.

158
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:36,860
Great Scissors!

159
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,294
Keep those magma-covered paws
of yours off of Straw Boy!

160
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:45,177
This kid is history, and
his father will be next!

161
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:48,120
Hell-wing-ga!

162
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,949
He's been pushing
himself since Impel Down.

163
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,520
He's passed his limit
physically and emotionally.

164
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,824
It's a wonder he's still alive.

165
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:06,315
One more hiccup and we could lose him.

166
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,953
If something were to happen on my watch,

167
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:12,117
I could never show my giant
face to his father again.

168
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:15,880
As Dragon's comrade, it's my
duty to protect his family.

169
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,120
I feel the same.

170
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:20,880
You think you're hot stuff?

171
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:23,017
You ain't seen nothing yet, Magma Boy.

172
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:23,930
Why?

173
00:10:24,013 --> 00:10:25,360
Because this queen is on fire!

174
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:43,877
Ladies and gentlemen, mostly gentlemen,
we are grateful for your patience.

175
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:47,717
Captain Teach and his merry men
present to you a stunning spectacle,

176
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,976
the likes of which you've never seen.

177
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:52,420
One, two... Daddy!

178
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:59,460
What did he do?

179
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:05,300
He was doing something in there, but what?

180
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,976
The Whitebeard's body looks the same.

181
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,089
Blackbeard's too, I think.

182
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:15,160
It's been fun.

183
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:16,770
Huh?

184
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,137
The Warlord thing, I mean.

185
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,020
You played your part well.

186
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,040
But as you'll see I
don't need you anymore!

187
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:47,180
This one here you all know it's my
dark dark fruit power, but this?

188
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,700
Just watch!

189
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,080
No, it can't be!

190
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,300
An earthquake?

191
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:27,628
That's the power of the
Tremor Tremor fruit!

192
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:31,037
I thought if you had two
telephone powers you would die,

193
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:34,649
and how did you take them for
Whitebeard in the first place?

194
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,320
I can't believe you pulled it off!

195
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:42,500
He stole that power from Pops!

196
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:44,100
I know, but how?

197
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:45,811
That isn't normal, is it?

198
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:51,297
A hand of darkness to call forth the void.

199
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:55,197
A hand of light to shake the
heavens and rend the earth.

200
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,697
Both are mine.

201
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:59,900
And the world will tremble
with my every step.

202
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:03,580
Only a fool would dare defy me.

203
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:09,297
I don't know how he did it, but he did it.

204
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:11,857
You can't fake having a power like that.

205
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:14,520
But does he know that we don't? Damn!

206
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:17,434
Young, we beat Whitebeard, but so what?

207
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:20,380
It's even worse than before! But hold on.

208
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,897
I thought if you tried to get
a second Devil Fruit power,

209
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:25,077
then your body would, like, blow up.

210
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:27,920
Yeah, for normal people,
that's how it works.

211
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:31,877
But you know as well as I do
that teaches anything but normal.

212
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:36,254
And with that body of his, he can pull
a trick we couldn't even dream of.

213
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:40,277
He's probably been planning
this thing for ages now.

214
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:42,260
Got your attention now, Z!

215
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:48,880
This is a wake-up call to all the boring
peace-lovers, the half-assed pirates,

216
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:53,500
the fat-headed fools in world
government, the ignorant masses.

217
00:13:54,060 --> 00:13:55,137
This is a nightmare.

218
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:56,279
It just has to be.

219
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:59,020
We all must answer to the hand of fate.

220
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:06,500
And fate has chosen me
to conquer this world.

221
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,840
H-Seal's coming down!

222
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,220
Run for it!

223
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:21,660
Abandon your balls!

224
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,420
We're all gonna die!

225
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,257
It's over.

226
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:30,940
There's nothing left.

227
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:36,200
The pirates, they took everything we had.

228
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:40,097
Our citadel where we've watched
over these waters for centuries.

229
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:44,600
It's all crumbling down the
symbol of the Navy's strength.

230
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,580
This is a nightmare

231
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:57,337
Damn he planned this from
the very start didn't he?

232
00:14:57,420 --> 00:15:00,357
He betrayed Whitebeard, captured
Ace, and became a warlord.

233
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,558
All the force them into this battle!

234
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:08,780
Alright then, take a good luck, cuz you
ain't seen nothing like this before?

235
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:15,420
They can't stop him now.

236
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:16,760
No one can.

237
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,840
I can hardly blame them.

238
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:32,600
I'd be crying too if my
enemies had this kind of power.

239
00:15:33,980 --> 00:15:34,860
Now what?

240
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:37,397
Took some time, but this
is a hell of a payoff.

241
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:41,520
I got the whole world wrapped
around my finger you bastard

242
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,400
Hey, what's wrong?

243
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:51,120
You don't want to fight?

244
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,880
I'm right here

245
00:15:53,420 --> 00:15:57,000
If you let me get away
who knows what I might do?

246
00:15:57,620 --> 00:15:59,320
Okay, I warned ya

247
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,580
Now where to start?

248
00:16:04,860 --> 00:16:06,560
Oh, I know

249
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:11,200
How about I give
Marineford a burial at sea?

250
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:14,160
He wouldn't dare!

251
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:34,930
Sarkwave!

252
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:52,320
You can tear down our buildings,
but in time we will rebuild them.

253
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,900
But this island is different.

254
00:16:58,240 --> 00:17:00,417
It's more than a symbol of our strength.

255
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,740
It stands in the center of the world.

256
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:05,130
Admiral.

257
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:08,537
And that means if we
want to protect innocent

258
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:10,914
people from criminals such as yourself,

259
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:16,540
it must be our stronghold, so
its light can reach every corner.

260
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:19,380
Compassion is justice.

261
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:21,200
It defies chaos.

262
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:26,500
It doesn't perish, and it will
certainly not sink by your hand.

263
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:28,740
Turn to learn your place.

264
00:17:37,840 --> 00:17:42,320
Well that's a downright noble
sentiment, compassion or what have you.

265
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:44,620
Well, come on!

266
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:48,380
Let's see what you're made of.

267
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:02,700
That isn't good.

268
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,860
We bought you some time.

269
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:09,600
Get him out of here.

270
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:12,260
Good luck.

271
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:16,860
Oh, no!

272
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,960
Bad move, Chop.

273
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:21,360
Now get over here.

274
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,324
You're a pesky one, aren't you?

275
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:26,580
Nu-kama-ken-po, aesthetic technique.

276
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:29,180
This one's my fat suctioning fist.

277
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,640
I like it hot, baby!

278
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:40,120
This isn't a game dammit get the
hell out of my way or pay the price

279
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,220
Who's next?

280
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,700
Don't you dare, Akaido!

281
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:14,120
You'd be wise to run while you
can, I have no business with you!

282
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:21,600
I dare not face him on dry
land, but the sea will aid me!

283
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:31,820
The water, it's frozen solid!

284
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:34,300
Damn, Aokiji!

285
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:38,720
Here he comes!

286
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:45,720
Nowhere left to run, you bloated fish!

287
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:53,140
I'm helpless then!

288
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:54,600
Hand him over!

289
00:19:57,120 --> 00:19:59,200
I'm putting an end to this!

290
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:19,677
It looks like it went
straight through him it might

291
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:22,584
have been Straw Hat and
they're falling fast too

292
00:20:27,940 --> 00:20:29,940
Still have some fight left in you.

293
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:31,200
That's a pity

294
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:38,177
Forgive me, Luffy.

295
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:41,240
It seems that I couldn't uphold my vow.

296
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:46,020
You might have saved yourself instead
of condemning the both of you.

297
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:50,840
If you keep making me miss,
it won't be good for anyone.

298
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:54,560
A blow to the heart would
be quick and painless.

299
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:56,760
Better than this.

300
00:21:04,160 --> 00:21:08,454
The boy's got a hole in his chest You
sure you still want to protect him?

301
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:16,097
You know he's gonna die either way.

302
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:18,600
I refuse to let him perish.

303
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,460
He protected us.

304
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:48,237
They won't be up there long.

305
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:50,637
So catch them when they fall
and put them on our ship!

306
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:53,320
Why the sudden change of heart?

307
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,737
I say if you're going to protect
someone then do it right!

308
00:21:56,820 --> 00:22:01,702
I don't like either of you, but if you
screw this up, then you'll let the Navy win!

309
00:22:05,380 --> 00:22:07,060
Sorry, I blew it, guys!

310
00:22:07,380 --> 00:22:11,197
You had so much faith in me, but I was
nothing more than a coward all along!

311
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:13,897
I'll just float away somewhere
and find a hole to crawl in,

312
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:16,377
because the only thing I'm
the king of is to survive it!

313
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:18,166
Oh crap, you're getting away!

314
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:26,994
They're stuck in here?

315
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,800
Wait, what's happening here?

316
00:22:29,940 --> 00:22:31,660
Nice catch, Captain Page!

317
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:33,880
You saved Straw Hat and Jimmy!

318
00:22:35,260 --> 00:22:37,640
I never should have doubted you!

319
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,600
He wasn't running!

320
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,897
He was just looking out for Straw Hat!

321
00:22:41,980 --> 00:22:43,997
Because all the glory in the world means

322
00:22:44,080 --> 00:22:46,786
nothing compared to the
life of an old friend!

323
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:48,920
How beautiful!

324
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:53,180
His heart's as pure as a baby lamb! Huh?

325
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:56,954
I can't hear what they're
saying, but I bet it's stupid.

326
00:22:57,340 --> 00:22:58,260
Huh? Jinbei?

327
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,440
And Straw Hat?

328
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:00,430
What the hell?

329
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:03,397
What are you idiots doing
all the way up here,

330
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:05,037
and why are you both covered in blood?

331
00:23:05,120 --> 00:23:06,897
This is weird, even for you guys.

332
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:08,980
Also, is it just me, or is it hot?

333
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:12,150
Ah!

334
00:23:12,233 --> 00:23:13,063
That's Madmon!

335
00:23:16,660 --> 00:23:18,580
Thank you, my red-nosed friend.

336
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:20,357
You saved our lives.

337
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:21,499
We're not friends.

338
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,577
I don't even know what's
going on right now.

339
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:26,560
I'm afraid I allowed Luffy to be harmed.

340
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:28,154
We must find a doctor.

341
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:30,260
He was burned quite badly.

342
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:31,860
I don't care!

343
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:34,857
And good luck finding a doctor
in the middle of this mess.

344
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:37,352
I had to trump the both of you right now.

345
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,796
Wait, were you making fun of my nose?

346
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:43,357
How many people do I have to
go through to finish that brat?

347
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:44,620
Rolls Rundle!

348
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:54,540
You're fools, each and every one of you.

349
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:59,197
Is one boy so damned important that
you're willing to throw your lives away?

350
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:01,280
You may mock us if you please,

351
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:03,957
but there is a strength
in Straw Hat's tenacity

352
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,393
that may prove invaluable to this world.

353
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:08,140
Pop spent his life on him.

354
00:24:08,380 --> 00:24:10,580
He has to carry on Ace's legacy.

355
00:24:11,180 --> 00:24:15,097
This is the dawn of a new era, and
we have a duty to see him through it.

356
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:21,100
Noble sentiment from a bunch of criminals,
but in the end, it's just empty talk.

357
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:30,000
I won't hesitate to strike you down.

358
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:31,360
Same here.

359
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:36,229
Your insistence on killing Straw Hat
just proves to us how much you fear him.

360
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:39,237
And if a tough guy like you
is scared of a boy like him,

361
00:24:39,320 --> 00:24:41,077
that means he's worth protecting.

362
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:42,900
To the death, if need be!

363
00:24:43,420 --> 00:24:46,600
Uh, can't you jackasses do
anything without my help?

364
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,280
Hey, are you even listening to me?

365
00:24:50,100 --> 00:24:52,100
You didn't just pass out, did you?

366
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:55,157
Hey, I didn't need it, buddy.

367
00:24:55,240 --> 00:24:56,157
Don't die on me.

368
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:57,997
Come on, you gotta tell me where to go.

369
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,860
I'm lost here. Help!

370
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:05,465
Frankly, I should be applauding
him for making Straw Hat suffer.

371
00:25:05,900 --> 00:25:09,457
But I suppose the pirate in me
would rather punch him in the face.

372
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:13,720
I see that trying to reason
with you is a lost cause.

373
00:25:15,620 --> 00:25:17,200
Have it your way.

374
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:32,460
This is too much.

375
00:25:33,180 --> 00:25:36,220
It's Sengoku versus Blackbeard over there.

376
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:46,180
And it's Aka-Inu versus the
commanders on that side.

377
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:55,520
I thought this war was
supposed to be over.

378
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:58,560
Captain Buggy, do something, anything.

379
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:00,846
I've got my hands full, okay?

380
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:11,260
What is that?

381
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:12,740
It was underwater.

382
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:14,150
A ship?

383
00:26:14,340 --> 00:26:15,680
It's a submarine.

384
00:26:16,660 --> 00:26:18,013
That's a Charlie Roger.

385
00:26:21,980 --> 00:26:22,810
Huh?

386
00:26:22,893 --> 00:26:24,760
I don't take orders from you, pal.

387
00:26:25,140 --> 00:26:28,552
And besides, what do you want
with him anyway, you weirdo?

388
00:26:28,780 --> 00:26:30,604
Actually, who the hell are you?

389
00:26:30,980 --> 00:26:35,333
Straw Hat may be my enemy someday, but
I'll let the fates decide that one.

390
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:38,424
Either way, it'd be a
waste to let him die here.

391
00:26:38,640 --> 00:26:40,477
Hand him over and we can escape.

392
00:26:40,560 --> 00:26:43,640
He'll die without my help! What?

393
00:26:50,520 --> 00:26:52,700
Trust me, I'm a doctor
